Subject: [PATCH] login: one SSO option per identity provider, sent to a browser-facing Keystone

GET /api/v1/sso builds the sign-in links the Skyline console offers, and
in stable/2026.1 it gets two things wrong for a deployment whose browsers
reach Keystone at another address from the one skyline-apiserver uses.

1. The links are built from [openstack] keystone_url. That is the address
   skyline-apiserver itself calls Keystone at, which kolla-ansible sets to
   the internal endpoint (http://<internal fqdn>:5000/v3/). A browser
   cannot reach it, and it is not the host whose mod_auth_openidc redirect
   URI the identity provider holds, so even where it resolves the sign-in
   fails at the provider. Nothing upstream addresses this.

   Add sso_keystone_url, the Keystone address the browser is sent to for
   SSO, used in place of keystone_url to build the links when it is set.
   It is an Optional[HttpUrl]: a URL is validated as keystone_url is, and
   unset (or an empty YAML value, which loads as null) keeps keystone_url,
   so the default behaviour is unchanged. keystone_url still serves every
   server-side call, including the websso token exchange.

2. The links use Keystone's protocol-level endpoint,
   /v3/auth/OS-FEDERATION/websso/{protocol}. Behind mod_auth_openidc that
   shows the module's bare provider-picker page, outside Skyline, instead
   of going to the identity provider.

   Backport skyline-apiserver master 60e2692e2b ("Return one SSO login
   option per identity provider"), which adds sso_identity_providers, a
   list of {name, protocol, label}. When it is set /sso returns one option
   per identity provider, pointing at the per-IdP endpoint
   /v3/auth/OS-FEDERATION/identity_providers/{idp}/protocols/{protocol}/websso,
   which redirects straight to the provider, with its label for the
   console to show; when it is empty the per-protocol options are kept.
   Also backport the runtime part of 170638b7a6 ("Improve
   sso_identity_providers docs and /sso response safety"): /sso is
   answered with response_model_exclude_none, so an option without a label
   carries no "label": null, which the stable/2026.1 console spreads over
   its computed option name and would blank it; and the option
   descriptions say sso_protocols is ignored while sso_identity_providers
   is set. Their tests, documentation and release notes are not installed
   in site-packages and are left out.

The configuration loader validates each option's value against its
schema but keeps the value as loaded from YAML, so sso_identity_providers
holds a list of mappings and is read as idp["name"], as upstream reads
it. The loader reads only the options it declares and ignores any other
key, so this image runs with a skyline.yaml written before or after it.

Applied against the installed copy in the venv, because the
skyline-apiserver Dockerfile runs kolla_patch after `pip install
/skyline-apiserver`. Paths use the version-independent `python3` symlink
created in docker/openstack-base/Dockerfile.j2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
